# Markdown Table Formatting

Always format markdown tables with aligned columns using consistent padding so they are readable in plain text, not just when rendered.

```markdown
| Field         | Example           |
| ------------- | ----------------- |
| IP Address    | 10.0.0.7          |
| Subnet Mask   | 255.255.255.240   |
| Gateway       | 10.0.0.1          |
```

Not:

```markdown
| Field | Example |
|---|---|
| IP Address | 10.0.0.7 |
| Subnet Mask | 255.255.255.240 |
| Gateway | 10.0.0.1 |
```

Rules:
- Pad every column so all `|` separators align vertically
- Use dashes in the separator row that match the column width (e.g. `| ------------- |`)
- Keep one space of padding on each side of every cell's content
